    "notes": "0.6 mm nozzle, 0.45 mm layers. Speeds are inherited from the 0.4 Speed profile and are deliberately generous: the governing limit is filament_max_volumetric_speed on the filament profile, which Orca enforces while slicing. Run Orca's Max Volumetric Speed calibration on this machine, then raise that ONE number and every profile here speeds up. Acceleration is intentionally not emitted - set it in firmware (M204 S#### then M500). TRAVEL SPEED: capped at 150 mm/s deliberately. CoreXY drives one motor at v*sqrt(2) on a 45-degree move, and the firmware's per-actuator ceiling is 316.7 mm/s (alpha/beta_max_rate 19000 mm/min) - so any travel above 224 mm/s overruns a motor on diagonals. An earlier 250 mm/s setting caused a real print failure: cumulative diagonal layer shift. Raise only after testing, and never above 224.",
